#   DAiSEE (bored): A. Gupta, A. D'Cunha, K. Awasthi, V. Balasubramanian, "DAiSEE: Towards User Engagement
#     Recognition in the Wild," arXiv:1609.01885, 2016; and A. Kamath, A. Biswas, V. Balasubramanian,
#     "A Crowdsourced Approach to Student Engagement Recognition in e-Learning Environments," WACV 2016.
#   UTA-RLDD (tired): R. Ghoddoosian, M. Galib, V. Athitsos, "A Realistic Dataset and Baseline Temporal
#     Model for Early Drowsiness Detection," CVPRW 2019.
#   CEW (eyes closed): F. Song, X. Tan, X. Liu, S. Chen, "Eyes Closeness Detection from Still Images with
#     Multi-scale Histograms of Principal Oriented Gradients," Pattern Recognition 47(9), 2014.
#   LFW (eyes open): G. B. Huang, M. Ramesh, T. Berg, E. Learned-Miller, "Labeled Faces in the Wild,"
#     UMass Amherst Tech. Report 07-49, 2007; and G. B. Huang, V. Jain, E. Learned-Miller, "Unsupervised
#     Joint Alignment of Complex Images," ICCV 2007.
#   Columbia Gaze (gaze): B. A. Smith, Q. Yin, S. K. Feiner, S. K. Nayar, "Gaze Locking: Passive Eye
#     Contact Detection for Human-Object Interaction," UIST 2013.
#   RT-GENE (gaze): T. Fischer, H. J. Chang, Y. Demiris, "RT-GENE: Real-Time Eye Gaze Estimation in
#     Natural Environments," ECCV 2018.
#   Face tracking: Google MediaPipe Face Landmarker (Apache 2.0 licence).


